<% content_for :title, "Privacy" %>
<h1>Privacy</h1>

<p>Gear Tracker keeps what you enter so you can see what your things really cost. It isn't used for anything else.</p>

<h2>What's stored</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Your account:</strong> your email address and your password, which is stored only as a one-way hash, so nobody can read it. If you set them, also a display name and username.</li>
  <li><strong>What you enter:</strong> your gear, expenses, fuel and energy entries, readings, notes and settings.</li>
  <li><strong>Sign-ins:</strong> for each signed-in browser, its IP address and browser name, so a session can be recognized.</li>
  <li><strong>API tokens:</strong> their names and when they were last used. The tokens themselves are stored only as a fingerprint.</li>
  <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> requests, with IP addresses, kept briefly to keep the site running and safe. Passwords and tokens are never logged.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What isn't done</h2>
<ul>
  <li>No ads, no tracking and no analytics. The only cookies are the ones that keep you signed in and protect your forms.</li>
  <li>Your data is never sold or shared, except with the services needed to run the site, listed below.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Services the site uses</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Email:</strong> password reset emails are sent through an email delivery service, which sees your email address and the message.</li>
  <li><strong>Backups:</strong> the database is copied continuously to encrypted cloud storage, so it can be restored if the server fails.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Your choices</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Public profile:</strong> off by default. If you turn it on in Settings, anyone with the link sees your display name, username and only the gear you mark public, with its costs only if you choose. Your email and other gear are never shown. Public pages ask search engines not to list them.</li>
  <li><strong>Download your data</strong> at any time from Settings, as a JSON file.</li>
  <li><strong>Delete your account</strong> from Settings. Everything you entered is deleted at once. Copies in backups are deleted as old backups expire, within <%= Rails.configuration.x.backup_retention_days %> days.</li>
</ul>

<p class="muted">Questions? Open an issue on <%= link_to "the project's GitHub page", "https://github.com/ticmyvom/gear-tracker" %>.</p>
